    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba715bbd_6d9a6527",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T13:47:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Secure should check this for us, no?",
      "parentUuid": "c42d030b_1d125e9c",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dd2b7577_9a98dfcb",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T13:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It will check the receiver ID I guess, I\u0027m not sure what it does if the receiver ID is for a non-secure VM. I don\u0027t think it will check the sender ID, it\u0027s up to the non-secure world to do that for non-secure senders.",
      "parentUuid": "ba715bbd_6d9a6527",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3881358b_1eb1efe5",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T14:53:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed. When we\u0027re exposing FF-A to pKVM guests, then we will need to look at this. But right now, I do not see the need.",
      "parentUuid": "dd2b7577_9a98dfcb",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b6da5e7_22c6acd7",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T15:31:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t trust the host, so we shouldn\u0027t let it spoof the ID of another entity.",
      "parentUuid": "3881358b_1eb1efe5",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a668d520_8720fc7c",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T17:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which other entity? The only other entities are secure, and EL3 must check for those.",
      "parentUuid": "8b6da5e7_22c6acd7",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ab8725a_f311fa3e",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 282,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T13:40:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The host could pretend that a VM is sending the memory. This shouldn\u0027t actually cause an issue by itself, as the secure world should know that there is no such VM, but perhaps it could be combined with some other bugs, so I\u0027d be happier if the hypervisor at least checked that the sender ID was the correct ID for the host and refused to send it on if not.",
      "parentUuid": "a668d520_8720fc7c",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d5a5bfa_66cacc94",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 299,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T12:21:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Check that there aren\u0027t any unsupported flags, e.g. CLEAR, or access modes we don\u0027t support or that aren\u0027t allowed, so the caller doesn\u0027t think we\u0027re doing something we\u0027re not.",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c76ff93_0273a469",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 299,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T13:47:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Again, won\u0027t secure handle these?",
      "parentUuid": "7d5a5bfa_66cacc94",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7251886_90cd942a",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 299,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T13:36:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think it handles clearing pages. I\u0027m not sure how much other validation it does, I haven\u0027t looked at the code in a while but from memory I thought it was fairly minimal and relied on the hypervisor to do most of the work. In any case, it\u0027s safer to have duplicate checks than miss them, right?",
      "parentUuid": "1c76ff93_0273a469",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "107ac38f_befb6541",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 299,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T14:53:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be strange not to handle clearing pages at EL3 -- doesn\u0027t that mean that clearing doesn\u0027t work when there isn\u0027t a hypervisor? In any case, for now I think we should keep this as minimal as we can and extend it only as features are actually required.",
      "parentUuid": "e7251886_90cd942a",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1292123_ea6a8ef0",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 299,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T15:31:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not saying you should handle it, I\u0027m just saying you should check that there aren\u0027t any unsupported features (such as clearing) being requested, and return an error if so.",
      "parentUuid": "107ac38f_befb6541",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca0a557b_f579cb64",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 299,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-10T17:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t that what currently happens? If clearing is requested and EL3 supports clearing, then the clearing will be handled by EL3. If it doesn\u0027t, then an error will be returned by virtue of us just forwarding the calls/responses between EL1 and EL3.\n\nWhy do we need to care whether EL3 supports these optional features if we are not relying on them?",
      "parentUuid": "b1292123_ea6a8ef0",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c15198df_7d721b57",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 299,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T13:40:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess my philosophy here (and in general) is essentially defence in depth, I\u0027d rather have more checks than necessary than not enough.",
      "parentUuid": "ca0a557b_f579cb64",
      "revId": "ca0b13e5963f51cb6bf7b0b624c0338e9e323e3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
  ]
}